================================================================================
(A) BINDING-PAIR MECHANISM: M(S) is a 2-body switch at a crossing tau*=k/(v_a +- v_b)
================================================================================

  TIGHT AP {1..13}: M=1/14, tau*=5/14
    binding runners (||v tau*|| == M): [3, 11]  (2 of them)
    binding PAIR (a,b)=(3,11); tau* = 5/(v_a+v_b) = 5/14  (a 2-body crossing)
      sum form: at tau*, runner 3 and runner 11 are on OPPOSITE sides equidistant from 0 (v_a+v_b=14)
    => the LRC optimum is decided by ONE pair, not by all 13 runners.

  hardcore 84: M=7/89, tau*=37/89
    binding runners (||v tau*|| == M): [5, 84]  (2 of them)
    binding PAIR (a,b)=(5,84); tau* = 37/(v_a+v_b) = 37/89  (a 2-body crossing)
      sum form: at tau*, runner 5 and runner 84 are on OPPOSITE sides equidistant from 0 (v_a+v_b=89)
    => the LRC optimum is decided by ONE pair, not by all 13 runners.

  drop6 u98: M=9/109, tau*=19/109
    binding runners (||v tau*|| == M): [11, 98]  (2 of them)
    binding PAIR (a,b)=(11,98); tau* = 19/(v_a+v_b) = 19/109  (a 2-body crossing)
      sum form: at tau*, runner 11 and runner 98 are on OPPOSITE sides equidistant from 0 (v_a+v_b=109)
    => the LRC optimum is decided by ONE pair, not by all 13 runners.

